{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5CZdaMiyEaJgDP3iqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism shifts. Tumblers fall into place with a resonant click that echoes through stone corridors older than memory.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\nBeyond me: a corridor of cold blue light. The air that rushes past carries the smell of rain on dust, of pages never turned, of a fire that burned out centuries ago and somehow still warms.\n\nThe floor beyond my threshold is worn smooth by feet that came before yours. The walls breathe faintly — expanding, contracting — as if the space itself has been waiting, alive, patient.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI do not ask where you are going. I do not ask why you have come. The key was enough. The key is always enough.\n\nBut know this: I open only once for each visitor. What you carry through me, you keep. What you leave behind, you lose.\n\n*The hinges hold. The passage is clear. The blue light pulses, gently, like a heartbeat.*\n\nStep through, or step away.\n\nI will not wait forever.\n\n*I will not close until you choose.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":242,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}